https://apidocs.lighter.xyz/docs/evm-int.content:
The Lighter protocol supports message passing across all three of its domains.
EVM and Core
communicate through stateful write streams, one in each direction. These streams are
settled on L1
together with Core and EVM state, allowing the sequencer to fulfill cross-domain write requests without waiting for L1 finality.
Message passing between
L1 and Core
and between
L1 and EVM
goes through the
ZkLighter
bridge on L1. The bridge maintains a separate priority queue for messages sent from L1 to each domain. It also handles messages arriving on L1 from Core and EVM, called
L1 calls
.
A batch may contain many
L1 calls
generated by Core and EVM. Once such a batch has been
executed on L1
, anyone can call the bridge to execute the included L1 calls. Batch execution makes the calls eligible but does not execute them itself.
Each
L1 Call
carries the following fields.
Solidity
struct L1Call {
    // Sender on the originating domain, authenticated by the bridge.
    address l2Sender;

    // L1 address to call.
    address to;

    // Amount of ETH to send with the call, in wei.
    uint256 value;

    // Nonce that distinguishes this call from other calls.
    uint256 msgNonce;

    // Calldata to pass to the L1 target.
    bytes data;
}
